<h2>Fntkech Under Desk Elliptical Features to Check</h2>
<p>Because listings under the Fntkech name vary, judge any model on the features below rather than on the product photos.</p>
<h3>1. Pedal height and desk clearance</h3>
<p>This is the number one reason people return under desk ellipticals. Your knees rise as the pedals reach their highest point. If your desk is low, they hit the desk. Measure first with our <a href="/tools/desk-clearance-checker/">desk clearance checker</a>.</p>
<h3>2. Resistance type</h3>
<p>Magnetic resistance is quiet and smooth. Friction or strap resistance is cheaper but louder and wears out. If the listing does not say "magnetic," assume it is not.</p>
<h3>3. Noise</h3>
<p>If you take calls, you want a machine that is close to silent. Cheaper units often squeak after a few weeks. Our <a href="/quietest-under-desk-elliptical/">quietest under desk elliptical</a> guide covers the models that stay quiet.</p>
<h3>4. Manual vs motorized</h3>
<p>Motorized versions move your legs for you. They are great for circulation and limited mobility but burn fewer calories unless you pedal along. Manual models give you more of a workout. See <a href="/manual-under-desk-elliptical/">manual under desk ellipticals</a> and the <a href="/best-motorized-under-desk-elliptical/">best motorized under desk ellipticals</a>.</p>
<h3>5. Seller, warranty and returns</h3>
<p>With lesser-known names, the seller matters more than the product page. Look for a return window of at least 30 days, a stated warranty and recent reviews that mention customer service.</p>
